 ## Background
-The method was introduced as a new intersection algorithm to address the trade-off between speed and correctness in ray-voxel intersection for isosurface rendering [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the observation that repeated linear interpolation is reliable if the starting interval contains exactly one root [S1, unofficial]. By isolating roots via extrema, it guarantees this condition. The method is well-suited for data parallel SIMD implementations, as it avoids the complex control flow of analytical solvers like Schwarze's [S1, unofficial].
